From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hjviewer <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 02:28:43 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 093/160] hjviewer: review fixes, words lane (1.9)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

U34: the administrator's wording ("HJViewer 관리자: <contact>") lives once, in
hjvAdminContactText; HjvTexts.adminContact and HjvUpdateText.contact call it.
The About screen's reading path moves to lane C's hjv-admin-contact reader
when that lands (critic X-13; integration checklist I-1).

U31: the pilot notice keeps the user's own wording; its rewording was not
decided (p2 D2) and is left to the user.

D-6/S-01: the logout dialog's remote line in English says that logging out
ends a password-less connection; the Korean cell is a release-blocking
checklist item for its owner, together with lane A's D-6.

U27: a pwless state this app does not know shows the server's note as it
came, so a later hjv-api does not blank the cards.

U28: the restart question gets "?" in a language whose text has none.

U35: the update screens' language is HjvHost.korean, which the gate test's
host pins to Korean.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
